height:120%">The principal considerations for our determination that perfor=
ming procedures relating to the valuation of inventories, specifically the =
provisions for excess or obsolete inventories and excess product purchase c=
ommitments, is a critical audit matter are the significant judgment by mana=
gement when developing provisions for excess or obsolete inventories and ex=
cess product purchase commitments, including developing assumptions related=
 to future demand and market conditions. This in turn led to significant au=
ditor judgment, subjectivity, and effort in performing procedures and evalu=
ating management=92s assumptions related to future demand and market condit=
ions.</span></div><div style=3D"margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify"><span=
